<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.8.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00504</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.8.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>dcc320a2-3d87-4f6d-882d-94d2e0c1acf4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 – 2, use the following passage:</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>A runner is training for a marathon. She runs more than 4 days each week. Each day, she runs between 12 and 15 miles. The marathon is 3 months away at the most.</para>
</blockquote>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="0ca15f01-7b3c-49e2-a528-491f804852e2"><problem><para>
      <para> What does the inequality \(d &gt; 4\) represent? </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>the number of miles in a marathon</para><para>the number of miles the runner runs each day</para><para>the number of months away the marathon is</para><para>the number of days the runner runs each week</para></problem><solution><para>the number of days the runner runs each week</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is the number of days the runner runs each week. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><para>For 3 - 8, write an inequality to represent the constraint given. </para>

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="04452122-a496-4774-88f1-f37f209b48b8"><problem><para>
      <para> There are less than 4 patients, \(p\), in the waiting room. </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(p &lt; 4 \)</para><para>\(p &gt; 4 \)</para><para>\(p\;\leq\;4\;\)</para><para>\(p\;\geq\;4\;\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(p &lt; 4 \)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(p\;&lt;\;4\;\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="21948567-9795-45ab-ba5c-d269cd4e7474"><problem><para>
      <para> The basket has between 12 and 19 eggs, \(e\). </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(12 &gt; e\) and \(\;e\;\;&gt;\;19\;\)</para><para>\(12\;\geq\;e\;\)and\(\;e\;\geq\;19\;\)</para><para>\(e\;\leq\;19\;\)</para><para>\(12\;≤\;e\;≤\;19\;\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(12\;≤\;e\;≤\;19\;\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(12 ≤ e ≤ 19\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="57a2b48e-e646-40cd-a130-2bda02cb8b94"><problem><para>
      <para> The total sales of tickets to a show is more than $68. An adult ticket, <emphasis effect="italics">a</emphasis>, costs $8 and a children’s ticket, \(c\), is $3. </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(8a\;+\;3c\;\leq\;68\;\)</para><para>\(8a\;+\;3c\;\geq\;68\;\)</para><para>\(8a + 3c &lt; 68 \)</para><para>\(8a + 3c &gt; 68 \)</para></problem><solution><para>\(8a + 3c &gt; 68 \)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(8a + 3c &gt; 68\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><para>For 9 - 11, use the following passage: </para>
<blockquote>
  <para>A doctor sees between 7 and 12 patients each day. On Mondays and Tuesdays, the
    appointment times are 15 minutes. On Wednesdays and Thursdays, they are 30 minutes long. On Fridays, they are one hour long. The doctor works for no more than 8 hours a day. Here are some inequalities that represent this situation. </para>
</blockquote>
<para>\(0.25\;\leq\;y\;\leq\;1\)            \(7\;\leq\;x\;\leq\;12\)           \(xy\;\leq\;8\)</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="80586fbc-b2d8-421d-acc7-0fadf313b894"><problem><para>
      <para> What does the variable <emphasis effect="italics">x</emphasis> represent? </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>the number of patients the doctor sees each day.</para><para>the part of an hour that each appointment lasts.</para><para>the total time the doctor spends working with patients each day.</para><para>the number of patients the doctor sees in a week.</para></problem><solution><para>the number of patients the doctor sees each day.</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is the number of patients the doctor sees each day. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><para>For 12 - 14, use the following passage:</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>Arnav wants to build a dog house. He makes a list of the materials needed:</para>
  <list>
    <item>At least 60 square feet of plywood for the surfaces</item>
    <item>At least 36 feet of wood planks for the frame of the dog house </item>
    <item>Between 1 and 2 quarts of paint</item>
  </list>
  <para>Arnav's budget is $65. Plywood costs $0.70 per square foot, planks of wood cost $0.10 per foot, and paint costs $8 per quart.</para>
</blockquote>

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="bc2297ed-28d8-428f-b938-3a65cf880bf6"><problem><para>
      <para> Which inequality represents the square feet of plywood needed? </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(p\;\geq\;60\)</para><para>\(p\;\geq\;36\)</para><para>\(1\;\leq\;p\;\leq\;2\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(p\;\geq\;60\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(p\;\geq\;60\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
